> (Related question: Is there a way to output the configured value of the new ForeignKeyMode via a SQL query?)

@reporter I have made a PR that adds a new query like `SHOW VSCHEMA KEYSPACES` and that might be the solution - https://github.com/vitessio/vitess/pull/14505, because this will just allow you to run a query and it will tell you exactly what the foreign key mode is that vitess is running in.

If you don't add a Vschema and are running with `--foreign-key-mode=allow`, then it would be `unmanaged` otherwise it would be `managed` as we see in the description of the PR.
